NAME

ulibStoreFileData - Allocates memory for and stores a file's description


SYNOPSIS

UBYTE *ulibStoreFileData(struct FileCat *f, UBYTE *Data)
                                 a0             a1


DESCRIPTION

This function allocates memory for the file description provided by <Data>
(which must be a null-terminated string), and links it to the file entry, <f>.

NOTE:  This routine does NOT look at what <f->Description> was previously, so
       if <f->Description> contained a previous file description, you will
       need to deallocate it before calling this function.

This routine allocates (strlen(Data)+1) bytes of memory for the description,
where the extra character is for the null terminator.


RETURNS

This function will return a pointer to the start of the memory allocated
<f->Description>, or NULL if not enough memory was available, or some other
error occurred.


SEE ALSO

ulibFreeFileData
